  "findings": [
    "City of Amery explicitly documents its marked canoe/kayak portage east of the dam. DNR landing coordinates and imagery confirm Birch Street above Amery Dam and Black Brook Flowage access above the separate downstream Black Brook Dam.",
    "Jefferson County moved its parks pages to parks.jeffersoncountywi.gov; current live links provide the county guide and segment maps. The current guide explicitly describes the Rome carry; older segment map also depicts the corridor but has stale Cushman-dam information. Current DNR inventory lists Cushman, Slabtown and Hebron removed; debris warnings remain.",
    "Added the county’s Hebron carry warning to the existing downstream map rather than treating a removed-dam record as hazard clearance.",
    "Hubbleton–Olson source course is 1.2507 miles against 1.3 planning miles; county guide gives 1.2 miles. Source vertices stay unchanged and display-only.",
    "County flood article names Kanow Park and Blackhawk Island Fishing Wharf; it does not close these reviewed Bark access points. No claim of current opening or hazard-free passage is made.",
    "Added Prince’s Point–Burnt Village overview: 6.8688 source miles vs unchanged 6.7 planning miles, 220 original vertices, no downstream forks. All ten course panels and both endpoint areas reviewed. County guide gives about 6.8 miles for the same access pair."
  ],
